From bb9f0eb86cfa455ac4bfd0bbc491af16cac49320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Haiku 5.5" <a@b>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:29:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rv1126b: device tree set for U-Boot (4 of 6)

Adds the RV1126B device tree set for U-Boot, from the kernel series' node set (rv1126b.dtsi,
the kernel series' patch 0006) plus the pin groups (rv1126b-pinctrl.dtsi, patch 0002):
- arch/arm/dts/rv1126b.dtsi, rv1126b-pinctrl.dtsi: the kernel files, unchanged.
- arch/arm/dts/rv1126b-u-boot.dtsi: the U-Boot overlay. bootph-all on cru, grf, ioc_grf, pinctrl,
  gpio0, gpio2, uart2, sdmmc0, and the sdmmc0 and uart2 pin groups and pcfgs SPL uses (the
  rk3576-u-boot.dtsi pattern); chosen u-boot,spl-boot-order = same-as-spl, sdmmc0.
- Reset numbers: include/dt-bindings/reset/rockchip,rv1126b-cru.h is the kernel series header
  (indices 0-327, the numbering the dtsi and the reset binding use). The seed's clock header
  also defined SRST_ names with different values (seed 1c535d65
  include/dt-bindings/clock/rockchip,rv1126b-cru.h), so those SRST_ lines and CLK_NR_SRST are
  removed from the U-Boot copy. Its CLK_ IDs are kept: the seed's clock driver uses them.
- drivers/clk/rockchip/clk_rv1126b.c: RV1126B_NR_SRST (328) replaces CLK_NR_SRST.
Checked: rv1126b.dtsi with the pin groups compiles with cpp and dtc, no warnings. The overlay
needs the generated config.h, so it is checked in the defconfig build (patch 5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
